    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0111" n="105" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg105"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860D.00/1004: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-07T18:00:00+02:00">December 7, 1942—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 8—8:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1202. Source<anchor n="83" xml:id="d114-f1"/> mentioned in my 1201 today<anchor
                        n="79" xml:id="d114-f2"/> said he thought Witting would be held in office as
                    long as Finland’s relationship of co-belligerency with Germany continued. He
                    admitted that there would be slight chance of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >rapprochement</hi> with us so long as Foreign Office <pb facs="0112"
                        n="106" xml:id="pg106"/> remained under Witting and Pakaslahti.… He added
                    that former prohibition on Foreign Office officials seeing members of this
                    Legation had recently been lifted. We reminded him that it took two to make a
                    party and that Foreign Office officials were not being invited by us except
                    rarely. Our friend said “the Finns have had more good luck than good ideas in
                    matters of foreign policy”. He seemed to think there was now neither good luck
                    nor good ideas.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d114-f1" n="83" xml:id="d114-f1-content">
                <p>The source of information was described as a “well informed member of Social
                    Democratic Party” of Finland.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d114-f2" n="79" xml:id="d114-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
